const KOBOLD_EN550={intro:'Among the smallest draconic creatures of the multiverse, kobolds reveal their ancestry through shining scales and powerful cries. Legends place the first kobolds in the Underdark near the lairs of the earliest dragons. Some serve or worship chromatic and metallic dragons; others help defend the world against draconic destruction.\n\nTheir scales are often rust-colored but can resemble the colors of chromatic or metallic dragons. Their cries express anger, determination, joy, fear, and other emotions, always carrying draconic power.',traits:[
 ['Creature Type','You are a Humanoid.'],['Size','You are Small.'],['Speed','Your walking speed is 30 feet.'],['Darkvision','You can see in dim light within 60 feet as if it were bright light, and in darkness as if it were dim light. You see colors in darkness only as shades of gray.'],['Draconic Cry','As a Bonus Action, you let out a cry at enemies within 10 feet of you. Until the start of your next turn, you and your allies have Advantage on attack rolls against those enemies that could hear you. You can use this trait a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.'],['Kobold Legacy','Choose one option.\n\nCraftiness. Gain proficiency in one of these skills: Arcana, Investigation, Medicine, Sleight of Hand, or Survival.\n\nDefiance. You have Advantage on saving throws to avoid or end the Frightened condition on yourself.\n\nDraconic Sorcery. Learn one cantrip of your choice from the Sorcerer spell list. Choose Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma as its spellcasting ability.'],['Languages','You can speak, read, and write Common and one other language that you and your Dungeon Master agree is appropriate. The Dungeon Master can adjust the campaign’s language list.']]};
