pairRule559(SAURIAN_INTRO556,'Saurians are scaled and feathered humanoids descended from dinosaurs and pterosaurs. Their colors express emotions, and their clans honor ancestors and collectively care for hatchlings. They reach adulthood at age 7 and can live as long as gnomes.\n\nChoose one of four lineages. All are Medium Humanoids with a walking speed of 30 feet.\n\n2024 compatibility: ability increases continue to come from your background, without stacking another increase from this species. The original book allows +1 to two different scores or +2 to one score. The older variant grants Intelligence +1 and lineage increases: Sharpfang, Dexterity +2; Leatherwing, Intelligence +1 and Charisma +1; Hammer-tail, Constitution +1 and Wisdom +1; Webfoot, Strength +1 and Wisdom +1. These older increases are reference only and are not applied automatically.');
pairRule559(DREAM_INTRO556,'Beyond the veil of reality, dreams shimmer with arcane power. You can draw upon the sleeping mind and bring its visions into the waking world. This magic may be a bloodline inheritance or a gift of fate.\n\nCodex 2024 adaptation: features originally gained at Sorcerer level 1 are gained at level 3. Later benefits retain levels 6, 14, and 18. At level 3, you also receive the spells the original table grants at levels 1 and 3.');
pairRule559(DREAM_INTRO2014_557,'Dream Sorcery · D&D 2014 Sorcerer.\n\nDream magic brings visions from the sleeping mind into the waking world. You gain Dream Sorcery Spells and Fate of Dreams at Sorcerer level 1. Later benefits arrive at levels 6, 14, and 18, following Planegea. This option does not grant Innate Sorcery.');
pairRule559(DRACONIC_SUB2014_557.text,'Your magic comes from draconic ancestry. Benefits are gained at Sorcerer levels 1, 6, 14, and 18, following the 2014 rules.');
